el_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nodejs/undici/actions/runs/40059449811/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nodejs/undici/actions/runs/40059449811/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nodejs/undici/actions/workflows/186182419","head_commit":{"id":"046bb4c6fe413a32ecb6d51eb3ecaa56c8c15b87","tree_id":"240cd8156d0ebe8ddcfe168b11c005debce4b9e2","message":"fix(h2): replay requests whose HEADERS raced a GOAWAY (#6065)\n\n* fix(h2): replay requests whose HEADERS raced a GOAWAY\n\nA stream opened before the client processes a GOAWAY but flushed after it is\nrefused by nghttp2 and surfaces as a frameError on the HEADERS frame. When the\nGOAWAY's lastStreamID covers the stream (2^31-1, the graceful shutdown notice\nhyper, Go and nghttp2 send), the request stays attached to the session and the\nframeError rejected it, although the peer never saw it.\n\nRequeue such requests when the body is replayable, within the GOAWAY replay\nbudget.\n\nRefs: https://github.com/nodejs/undici/issues/6064\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Mohamed Elsharnouby <mohamed@radar.com>\n\n* fix(h2): finalize GOAWAY state before closing streams\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Mohamed Elsharnouby <mohamed@radar.com>\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:43:10Z","author":{"name":"mohamed-rdr","email":"mohamed.elsharnouby@radar.com"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com"}},"repository":{"id":133092972,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkxMzMwOTI5NzI=","name":"undici","full_name":"nodejs/undici","private":false,"owner":{"login":"nodejs","id":9950313,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5NTAzMTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9950313?v=4","gravatar_id":""